isp: t41: name the module after its own SoC, not t40

kernel/isp/t41/Kbuild sets MODULE_NAME to tx-isp-t40, copied from the t40
directory it was derived from, so a T41 build installs tx-isp-t40.ko.

load_ingenic probes the module as tx-isp-${SOC}, so on T41 it looks for
tx-isp-t41 and finds nothing. Every other ISP directory names the module
after its own SoC; t10, t20 and t30 do it with $(SOC), which is used here
too.

Upstream: https://github.com/openipc/openingenic

Signed-off-by: Oskari Rauta <oskari.rauta@gmail.com>

--- a/kernel/isp/t41/Kbuild
+++ b/kernel/isp/t41/Kbuild
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-MODULE_NAME := tx-isp-t40
+MODULE_NAME := tx-isp-$(SOC)
 OUT := $(MODULE_NAME)

 DIR=isp/$(SOC)
